  "label": "User projected onto the scene of atomic bomb visualizations",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the overall scene, which includes both the visual material of atomic bomb designs and the textual material labeling it as a '3d visualization of atomic bomb'. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me', 'you', or 'your' in the text. The projection is implicit, as the user is expected to interpret the image as a technical visualization, and the scene as a whole is the object of their attention and understanding. The user is not projected onto a specific textual or visual element in isolation, but onto the entire labeled scene.",
